{"change_summary":"Completed the pending shrimp bookkeeping amendment pass by hardening the shared stage/egg cohort count helpers with saturating arithmetic and adding regression coverage for the remaining lifecycle invariants: hatch-into-empty juvenile reset, promotion into empty sub-adult reset, and multi-day population conservation where total population change equals births minus deaths. The current `tank_core` branch now has direct tests covering the empty-stage carryover bug class and the acceptance-criteria count-accounting identity.","outstanding_risks":["This amendment pass revalidated `tank_core` only; downstream crates were not rerun because the net code diff stayed inside that crate.","The new conservation regression isolates births and deaths by freezing stage promotions, so long-horizon accounting with simultaneous promotion and mortality still relies on the existing transition-specific tests rather than a dedicated combined invariant test."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspect the current branch to confirm which pending shrimp-stage amendments were already wired and where the remaining gaps still lived in shared biology helpers and regression coverage.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Harden the shared stage/egg cohort helper arithmetic so incoming-stage and egg-cohort totals use saturating count math instead of unchecked `u32` addition.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Add focused shrimp population regressions for hatch-into-empty juvenile state reset, promotion into empty sub-adult state reset, and multi-day births-minus-deaths population conservation.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Format the updated code and rerun the relevant `tank_core` validation suites, including the full crate test pass.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --lib` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test shrimp_population --test validation --test save_load` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed (full `tank_core` suite, including the new shrimp population regressions)."]}